y. From 1996 to 2006, the rate of outpatient colonoscopy procedures increased for adults aged ≥50 years. For persons aged 50-64 years, the rate in 2006 was 3.5 times higher than the rate in 1996 (472.4 versus 132.2 procedures per 10,000 population), and for those aged 65-74 years, the rate was nearly three times higher (638.5 versus 216.2). For persons aged 75-84 years, the rate in 2006 was more than twice the rate in 1996 (517.3 versus 230.5), and for persons aged ≥85 years, the increase was approximately double (173.6 versus 96.9).","hasAlt":true,"isDecorative":false,"isMissingAlt":false,"ariaHidden":false,"rolePresentation":false,"renderedWidth":609,"renderedHeight":331,"naturalWidth":609,"naturalHeight":331,"loading":null,"decoding":null,"altVerdict":"TOO_LONG","altReason":"alt text is 712 characters — consider a caption or description","bytes":16886},{"src":"https://www.cdc.gov/TemplatePackage/images/icon_pdf.gif","alt":"Adobe PDF file","hasAlt":true,"isDecorative":false,"isMissingAlt":false,"ariaHidden":false,"rolePresentation":false,"renderedWidth":16,"renderedHeight":16,"naturalWidth":16,"naturalHeight":16,"loading":null,"decoding":null,"altVerdict":"GOOD","altReason":"present, no red flags","bytes":6058},{"src":"https://www.cdc.gov/TemplatePackage/images/icon_word.gif","alt":"Microsoft Word file","hasAlt":true,"isDecorative":false,"isMissingAlt":false,"ariaHidden":false,"rolePresentation":false,"renderedWidth":16,"renderedHeight":16,"naturalWidth":16,"naturalHeight":16,"loading":null,"decoding":null,"altVerdict":"GOOD","altReason":"present, no red flags","bytes":1087},{"src":"https://www.cdc.gov/TemplatePackage/images/icon_excel.gif","alt":"Microsoft Excel file","hasAlt":true,"isDecorative":false,"isMissingAlt":false,"ariaHidden":false,"rolePresentation":false,"renderedWidth":16,"renderedHeight":16,"naturalWidth":16,"naturalHeight":16,"loading":null,"decoding":null,"altVerdict":"GOOD","altReason":"present, no red flags","bytes":644},{"src":"https://www.cdc.